&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;COPYRIGHT NOTICE&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NON-COMMERICIAL USE ONLY.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; Digital Sanborn Maps for Illinois are reproduced and distributed under exclusive license from ProQuest LLC and Environmental Data Resources, Inc. No portion of the map images may be downloaded, printed or otherwise retained for commercial purposes, including but not limited to environmental or other land use evaluations, without the prior consent of Environmental Data Resources, Inc.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; For information on how to obtain maps for commercial purposes, go to:&lt;br /&gt; Environmental Data Resources, Inc.&lt;br /&gt; 440 Wheelers Farms Road&lt;br /&gt; Milford, CT 06461&lt;br /&gt; 1-800-352-0050&lt;br /&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.edrnet.com&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #693a77; text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;http://www.edrnet.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; All copyright in the Sanborn Maps are held by Environmental Data Resources, Inc. or its affiliates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/cdm/search/collection/saskia&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #693a77; text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Browse all items in the collection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This archive is available to CARLI Governing member libraries at no direct cost to the library. &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; CARLI has purchased the Saskia digital image archive from Scholars Resource. For more information, see &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scholarsresource.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #693a77; text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;http://www.scholarsresource.com/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. The collection contains 30,000 digital images of paintings, sculpture and architecture, including images from many important collections: the Prado, the Kunsthistorisches Museum, the Uffizi, and the Louvre as well as archaeological sites in Greece, Italy, Turkey and Egypt. The images can be displayed and downloaded in high-resolution format. Additionally, the descriptive data about the images includes references to the occurrences of these images in 19 major art history texts, including Gardner&apos;s Art Through the Ages, 12th edition; Understanding Art, 7th edition; Art and Ideas, 10th edition; Discovering Art History, 4th edition. &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; A high-resolution TIFF version of each Saskia image is available. The TIFF can be downloaded directly from the metadata for any image via the link in the Full Resolution metadata field. Download methods vary across browsers, but clicking or right-clicking on the link should prompt a download or &quot;save as&quot; option. Please note that the TIFF images are high-resolution, and, consequently, have very large file sizes that may take several minutes to download. &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;/cdm/favorites&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #693a77; text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Favorites&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a cookie-based browser feature within CONTENTdm for users to save images and work with them. Users may wish to save their selected Favorites images for later use. A thumbnail view, links to the images, and item metadata can be saved as a PowerPoint presentation. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt; To browse the collection, click &quot;Browse collection&quot; from the menu bar at the top of the page. &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; To see images in the collection that are present in a specific textbook, select the title from the dropdown list.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
